.TH clean 1 0.2.11 https://github.com/dbowm91/cargo-cleanme "General Commands Manual"
.SH NAME
clean \- Preview or execute cleanup of revalidated Cargo build artifacts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBclean\fR [\fB\-\-known\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIROOT\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Preview or execute cleanup of revalidated Cargo build artifacts.
.PP
A hidden compatibility alias (ADR 008 §4b): the root is the canonical cleanup front door, and this subcommand keeps every published spelling working — `clean ROOT`, `clean \-\-known` and `clean \-\-full` — without advertising a second front door.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-known\fR
Clean bounded roots selected by the current Routine policy
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Application simulation: run the full decision/proof/report path but invoke no Cargo clean command. The default mode is Execute
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
